    "title": "Japanese Shipbuilders to Invest $2 Billion to Double Output",
    "text": "A group of Japanese shipbuilders is planning to invest over $2 billion to double the number of ships the country makes.\nThey aim to install large cranes and other facilities to shore up Japan’s shipbuilding base. The United States and Japan have stepped up their cooperation, following President Donald Trump’s pledge to counter China's dominance in shipbuilding.\nThe United States has started charging fees on Chinese-built ships that call at American ports.\nFollowing the move, some fleet owners have been rethinking orders from Chinese yards. Japanese shipyards have also been seeing a growing number of inquiries.",
